    "title": "Spider-Man: Brand New Day's Trailer Officially Unveils Scorpion & 3 Other Villains' Designs For The MCU Movie",
    "text": "Published Mar 18, 2026, 8:07 AM EDT Felipe Rangel is a Movie and TV Journalist ScreenRant. He has been writing about movies and TV since 2021. Felipe joined ScreenRant in 2022, working across different teams, covering everything from breaking news to features to reviews and more. Felipe is a writer who is an avid film and TV fan, with superhero movies and series being his biggest passion. He graduated from college in 2019, having studied Journalism. Before college, he spent a month studying at the Oxford English Centre. His superhero knowledge expands to the comics, with his undergraduate thesis being \"Politics Reflected In American Comics.\" Sign in to your Screen Rant account The Spider-Man: Brand New Day trailer has been released, and the Marvel Cinematic Universe movie has revealed the first look at several villains who will either return to the franchise or make their debut. The MCU's Spider-Man movies are getting an exciting new chapter, as Spider-Man: Brand New Day's story is set to completely rewrite Peter Parker's life in more ways than one. After Spider-Man: No Way Home brought back Tobey Maguire and Andrew Garfield's Spider-Men and villains from their solo movies, Spider-Man: Brand New Day's cast was put together with the intent of delivering a new entry that is just as exhilarating as what came before. That includes an excellent batch of villains, who fans have now seen a snippet of in the trailer. While Peter Parker is undergoing a mutation of sorts in Spider-Man: Brand New Day, Gargan will be on a different path, using technology to become Scorpion. With no helmet, the design looks like a more advanced version of Scorpion's suit in Marvel's animated Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man. Aside from Scorpion, three other villains appear in the trailer. Finally, the group of red ninjas seen at the end of the Spider-Man: Brand New Day trailer has to be The Hand, who MCU fans will recognize from Netflix's The Defenders Saga. This time around, The Hand gets even more vibrant red costumes than before, going for a comics-accurate approach. While reported for the MCU movie, Tombstone is absent from the trailer. Tombstone's absence from the Spider-Man: Brand New Day trailer also suggests that Marvel and Sony are choosing to hide him for now, which makes him look like the villain pulling the strings from the shadows. Will that be true? It remains to be seen, as a character who can mind-control people is also teased in the Spider-Man: Brand New Day trailer. Release Date July 31, 2026 Director Destin Daniel Cretton Writers Chris McKenna, Erik Sommers, Steve Ditko, Stan Lee",
